Z||000000||JetroGT||10-18-2000||05:44 PM||||I have a couple of questions on doing this. For one, how much does the new switch cost?<BR>Has any one replaced it before?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Reverseswitch.jpg0.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||the need for speed||10-18-2000||05:50 PM||||were the hell is it||||reg||1
Z||000002||PJ||10-18-2000||06:34 PM||||The switch is under the shift lever. It is just a contact switch and they do go bad. Just unscrew and replace. P/N is 10075403. BTW, you can use the switch off later Getrags if you can find one at the boneyard. You'll probably have to change the connector if you do.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||JimIndyRCR||10-18-2000||11:14 PM||||Howdy,<BR>I just purchased a back up switch from a local parts store- Delco part # AC D2219A. It was $15.00. It's difficult to get to but with the right wrench you can do it.<BR>Hope this helps.<BR>Jim||||reg||1
